{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1788458592544,"sessionID":"ses_f97919226ffeSaD2Vc16sHo0wL","part":{"id":"prt_068703127001WJv3j1h1V7b2Mh","messageID":"msg_068702024001i0joSwaB23iXVT","sessionID":"ses_f97919226ffeSaD2Vc16sHo0wL","type":"reasoning","text":"Good - the adapter passes `lm_kwargs` (which is `config`) directly to the LM call as `**lm_kwargs`. So `config[\"prediction\"]` will reach the LM call as `prediction=...` kwarg, which litellm passes through to OpenAI as the `prediction` parameter.\n\nNow let me write the tests. I'll add tests to `tests/predict/test_predict.py`:\n\n1. `test_prediction_passed_to_lm` — valid prediction format is moved to LM kwargs and removed from inputs.\n2. `test_invalid_prediction_treated_as_regular_input` — a prediction not matching the format stays in the inputs (and gets formatted as a regular input field, if it's part of the signature).\n\nLet me write the tests using a SpyLM pattern similar to existing tests.","time":{"start":1788458578215,"end":1788458592519},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Good - the adapter passes `lm_kwargs` (which is `config`) directly to the LM call as `**lm_kwargs`. So `config[\"prediction\"]` will reach the LM call as `prediction=...` kwarg, which litellm passes through to OpenAI as the `prediction` parameter.\n\nNow let me write the tests. I'll add tests to `tests/predict/test_predict.py`:\n\n1. `test_prediction_passed_to_lm` — valid prediction format is moved to LM kwargs and removed from inputs.\n2. `test_invalid_prediction_treated_as_regular_input` — a prediction not matching the format stays in the inputs (and gets formatted as a regular input field, if it's part of the signature).\n\nLet me write the tests using a SpyLM pattern similar to existing tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}}}
